    <string name="guide_welcome">A quick tour</string>
    <string name="guide_welcome_text">Where things are and how to turn on protection. It takes a minute, and you can skip it.</string>
    <string name="guide_settings">Settings</string>
    <string name="guide_settings_text">The menu button opens your account, new groups and channels, contacts and Settings. Settings start with Security and privacy, then Network and Tor, Appearance, Notifications and Account.</string>
    <string name="guide_security">Turn on protection</string>
    <string name="guide_security_text">In Security and privacy set a PIN to lock the app, keep screen capture protection on and hide names in notifications. The lock indicator shows whether a PIN is set.</string>
    <string name="guide_tor">Tor and bridges</string>
    <string name="guide_tor_text">Tor hides your IP address from the server: the app connects to its onion address. Bridges are unlisted Tor relays that help where Tor is blocked. The Tor indicator shows the state; tap it for network settings.</string>
    <string name="guide_contacts">Adding contacts safely</string>
    <string name="guide_contacts_text">Tap search and type a username to find a person. Get the username from them directly, then compare the safety number on their profile in person or over another channel.</string>
    <string name="guide_appearance">Make it yours</string>
    <string name="guide_appearance_text">Theme, motion, layout and message style are in Settings, Appearance. This guide can be opened again in Settings, About.</string>

